exercises.instructions:
Inheritance lets a child class share all properties and methods from a parent class. The child can also add new properties or override existing methods.

`extends` creates the parent-child relationship. `super()` in the child constructor calls the parent constructor to set up inherited properties.

Syntax:
```
class Parent {
  constructor(name) { this.name = name; }
  greet() { return "Hello"; }
}
class Child extends Parent {
  constructor(name, extra) {
    super(name);        // calls Parent constructor
    this.extra = extra; // add child-only property
  }
  greet() { return "Hi"; } // override parent method
}
```

